---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title={`Privacy and cookies | ${SITE_NAME}`} description="How Everest Base Camp Trek Guide uses cookies, Google Analytics and AdSense, and how to change or withdraw your consent.">
  <div class="wrap prose" style="padding-top: 56px; padding-bottom: 96px; max-width: 760px">
    <h1 class="h-display" style="font-size: 44px; margin-bottom: 24px">Privacy and cookies</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: 27 November 2026.</em></p>
    <p>This site is an independent guide to the Everest Base Camp trek. It is run by Focus Group SIA, Latvia, which is responsible for your data here. Contact: <a href="mailto:guide@everestbasecamptrekguide.com">guide@everestbasecamptrekguide.com</a>.</p>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>We do not ask you to register, and there are no comment or contact forms. The site does not collect your name, email address or other personal details directly.</p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web server, Cloudflare processes your IP address and basic request data to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse.</p>
    <h2>Analytics and ads</h2>
    <p>We use Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages are read, and Google AdSense to show ads that keep the site free. In the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland, these Google services only use cookies or similar storage after you agree in the consent message, which is managed by Google’s consent tool. If you do not agree, Google may still show non-personalised or limited ads.</p>
    <p>You can change or withdraw your choice at any time with “Cookie settings” at the bottom of every page. More about how Google uses data: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.</p>
    <p>We also use Ahrefs Web Analytics to count page views and see where visitors come from. It sets no cookies, does not store your IP address and does not follow you across websites or from one day to the next, so it runs without asking for consent. More about how it works: <a href="https://help.ahrefs.com/en/articles/10247870-about-ahrefs-web-analytics">help.ahrefs.com</a>.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>If GDPR applies to you, you can ask for access to, correction or deletion of your personal data, and you can complain to your data protection authority. Write to <a href="mailto:guide@everestbasecamptrekguide.com">guide@everestbasecamptrekguide.com</a>. In Latvia, the authority is the Data State Inspectorate (Datu valsts inspekcija).</p>
  </div>
</Base>
